  "notes": "The lane's jazz hinge, and the only entry in this batch the research rates plain `high` — gear, harmonic training and collaboration method are all directly sourced. Three parameters carry it. (1) Harmony: \"ii–V–I cycles, modal interchange, m9/maj7/altered dominants\" is the widest vocabulary in the section, so `extensions` puts 85% of the weight above the triad, `borrowed.V` is 0.35, and the families are functional rather than vamps. (2) Feel: **E-mu SP-1200** and **Casio CZ-101** are his named machines, and the SP-1200 lineage means \"crunchy, short, slightly-swung 12-bit drums … ride/hat played rather than gridded\" — that is `swing.grid` \"8th\" at 0.60, `quantizeStrength` 0.62, and the largest `timingJitterMs` on the hats of anything here. (3) Density: he declines a fixed sound (\"I try not to bring a *sound* to the table\") and instead includes everyone's part (\"Let's do all three of the parts!\"), which in practice is **dense multi-instrument layering with parts that answer each other** — hence `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.62 with `fillGapsOnly` false and three answering styles. ⚠ The alto saxophone is his signature lead voice and there is no sax `timbreHint` in the dataset; `horn_stab` is the nearest existing value and is a compromise, not a reading of the record. ⚠ The 808 is deliberately weak here — the research says he \"prefers played bass … where an 808 is used it is soft and short\", so `bass808.role` is `counter_riff` and the real low end is `bassline` as an `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.40 and walking cell shapes. ⚠ Key changes between sections are documented and are NOT modeled — the engine has one key per session. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.3 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.3 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 52 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3. ⚠ `countermelody.fillGapsOnly` returned to true. With it off and a density of 0.62, the counter plays THROUGH the melody rather than around it, and coherence.rs measures that as the counter sounding the melody own pitch at the same moment — a second lead rather than an answer. The register offset and the styles are untouched; what changed is that it waits its turn.",
